    "text": "Rachel Maddow suggested that the name of Vance’s venture capital company, Narya, was a nod to the word, ‘Aryan,'” That’s loony Rachel for you.\nNarya Capital, JD Vance’s venture capital firm co-founded in 2019 and based in Cincinnati, Ohio, derives its name from J.R.R. Tolkien’s The Lord of the Rings. Specifically, “Narya” refers to one of the three Elven Rings of Power, known as the Ring of Fire, which symbolizes inspiration, hope, and resistance against tyranny and despair.\nThis choice aligns with Peter Thiel’s influence, as Vance previously worked at Thiel’s Mithril Capital (named after the fictional metal mithril from Tolkien’s works). It’s part of a pattern in Thiel-backed firms using Tolkien-inspired names, reflecting a shared cultural nod among Silicon Valley investors.",
